---
/**
 * What is actually deployed, drawn from the two wrangler.jsonc files and the
 * two Worker entries rather than from a sketch.
 *
 * IT DISAGREES WITH 01 §2's ASCII DRAWING, DELIBERATELY. That diagram puts the
 * chat and analysis endpoints on the site Worker; they are on the MCP Worker,
 * because both need the `ai` binding and an `ai` binding cannot exist in the
 * config `astro build` instantiates (the CI failure is written up in both
 * wrangler.jsonc files). Publishing the spec's version on the page whose whole
 * premise is that its figures are checkable would be self-refuting -- the first
 * reader to `curl` the two endpoints would find the picture wrong.
 *
 * TWO CLAIMS IN THE FIRST DRAFT OF THIS FILE CAME FROM THAT SAME STALE DRAWING
 * AND WERE FALSE. Recorded rather than quietly replaced, because both are the
 * kind of detail a reader would actually reason from:
 *
 *   - "`/mcp` is a Durable Object" -- IT IS NOT. The endpoint is served by
 *     `createMcpHandler` (agents/mcp/server), which this repo's own comments
 *     twice describe as stateless: workers/mcp/src/index.ts builds "one
 *     instance per HTTP request", and workers/mcp/src/define.ts's whole
 *     `clientInfo` argument exists BECAUSE the server is rebuilt per request.
 *     That Worker declares exactly one Durable Object class and it is the rate
 *     limiter (workers/mcp/wrangler.jsonc's `RATE_LIMITER`/`RateLimiter`,
 *     sqlite migration v1, re-exported from index.ts). The rate limiter now has
 *     its own line, which is both true and the more interesting fact.
 *   - "Analytics Engine feeds the events queue" -- IT DOES NOT. They are two
 *     independent sinks written from the same handlers: AE through
 *     `env.AE.writeDataPoint` (src/lib/agent-intel/record.ts, fire and forget),
 *     the queue through `env.EVENTS.send` on the high-intent path
 *     (src/worker.ts, via `highIntentFor`). The consumer
 *     (src/lib/agent-intel/consume.ts) reads queue message bodies and never
 *     touches AE, and nothing in either Worker reads AE at all --
 *     src/lib/ops/analytics.ts's header says that binding "writes and cannot
 *     query", which is why /ops reads it over HTTPS instead.
 *
 * Every other claim re-verified 2026-09-11 against ./wrangler.jsonc,
 * workers/mcp/wrangler.jsonc, src/worker.ts, workers/mcp/src/index.ts,
 * src/pages/chat/send.ts, migrations/0001-0004 and the `gateway:` options on
 * the two `env.AI.run` calls in src/lib/{chat,fit}/engine.ts. The embedding path
 * carries no `gateway:` option, which is why only the Anthropic line names one.
 *
 * NO UNLISTED ROUTE IS NAMED HERE, and that is the one thing this diagram
 * deliberately leaves out. src/worker.ts flattens every refusal on the
 * token-scoped prefix into the site's own 404 precisely so that a stranger
 * cannot tell a real route from a dead one, src/lib/unindexed-routes.mjs keeps
 * it out of the sitemap and src/pages/llms.txt.ts out of the index -- and /ops
 * IS in the sitemap. Printing that path here would spend a documented
 * requirement and three mechanisms for one word on a drawing. "the form
 * surfaces" is the honest aggregate.
 *
 * INLINE SVG, NEVER AN `<img>`: the diagram has to follow the visitor's theme,
 * and an image cannot. Strokes are `currentColor` so the box work inherits the
 * ink token, the quieter lines take `--color-rule` through Tailwind's
 * `stroke-rule`, and there is no hex anywhere in this file.
 *
 * THE TYPE HAS A FLOOR, AND IT IS THE SCALE'S OWN MINIMUM. The drawing scales
 * rather than scrolls (`w-full` over a `viewBox`), so every label shrinks with
 * it -- and a first draft at 11.5 and 10 user units landed near 10.1 and 8.8
 * CSS px at a 400px viewport, under `--text-micro` (12px), the smallest size
 * global.css defines. The arithmetic that fixes it: a 400px viewport inside
 * `px-6` gives the svg 352px, so a user unit renders at 352/400 = 0.88px, and
 * nothing may be set below 12/0.88 = 13.6. Hence 14 for every label and 17 for
 * the box titles -- 12.3px and 15.0px at the small end, 15.7px and 19.0px at
 * `max-w-md`. Changing the viewBox width without redoing that division puts the
 * labels back under the floor.
 *
 * Line lengths are bounded by the same arithmetic: IBM Plex Mono advances
 * 0.6em, so a 14-unit line inside a 360-wide box with 12 units of padding fits
 * 40 characters. Every line below is at or under that.
 *
 * `<title>` and `<desc>` with `aria-labelledby` are what a screen reader gets;
 * `role="img"` stops it from walking the 40-odd shapes underneath.
 */
---

<figure class="mt-10">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 400 635"
    class="h-auto w-full max-w-md"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="architecture-title architecture-desc"
    fill="none"
  >
    <title id="architecture-title">How this site is deployed</title>
    <desc id="architecture-desc">
      Two Cloudflare Workers. Visitors and agents reach the site Worker at ryanlindsey.me, which
      serves the pages, posts, case studies and the résumé, prerendered with some routes rendered on
      demand, plus llms.txt, the markdown variants and the feeds; it hosts the chat page and the
      form surfaces, and runs the queue consumer that sends the notification email. It calls the MCP
      Worker at mcp.ryanlindsey.me over a service binding for the MCP endpoint, for chat and for
      form posts; the MCP Worker calls back the same way to read published documents. The MCP Worker
      serves the MCP endpoint statelessly, rebuilding the server for each request, alongside the
      streamed chat inference and the discovery routes; it holds the one Durable Object in this
      system, which enforces the rate limits, and it is where inference runs — through AI Gateway to
      Anthropic, and through Workers AI into Vectorize for retrieval. Both Workers share D1 for the
      audit log, tokens, transcripts and eval runs, KV for caches and flags, R2 for generated PDFs
      and documents, Analytics Engine for request telemetry, and a queue that carries high-intent
      events to the email. Analytics Engine and the queue are independent sinks; neither feeds the
      other.
    </desc>

    {/* Visitors and agents */}
    <rect x="90" y="4" width="220" height="40" class="fill-surface" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
    <text x="200" y="29" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" class="font-mono fill-current"
      >Visitors and agents</text
    >

    {/* ... down to the site Worker */}
    <path d="M200,44 L200,76" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M195,68 L200,76 L205,68" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <text x="208" y="64" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted">HTTPS</text>

    {/* The site Worker */}
    <rect x="20" y="76" width="360" height="146" class="fill-surface" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
    <text x="32" y="102" font-size="17" class="font-mono fill-current"
      >Site Worker &#183; ryanlindsey.me</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="128" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >Astro, prerendered and on demand</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="147" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >posts, case studies, the r&#233;sum&#233;</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="166" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >/llms.txt, .md variants, RSS and JSON</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="185" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >/chat page and the form surfaces</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="204" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >the queue consumer and the email send</text
    >

    {/* The binding cycle: site to MCP, and MCP back to the site */}
    <path d="M110,222 L110,278" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M105,270 L110,278 L115,270" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <text x="118" y="242" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted">/mcp, chat and forms</text
    >
    <path d="M290,278 L290,222" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M285,230 L290,222 L295,230" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <text x="282" y="268" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >document reads</text
    >

    {/* The MCP Worker */}
    <rect x="20" y="278" width="360" height="165" class="fill-surface" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
    <text x="32" y="304" font-size="17" class="font-mono fill-current"
      >MCP Worker &#183; mcp.ryanlindsey.me</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="330" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >/mcp endpoint, stateless per request</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="349" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >POST /chat, the streamed inference</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="368" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >/robots.txt, /.well-known/mcp.json</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="387" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >rate limits in a Durable Object</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="406" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >AI Gateway &#8594; Anthropic</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="425" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >Workers AI &#8594; Vectorize, for retrieval</text
    >

    {/* ... down to what both of them share */}
    <path d="M200,443 L200,483" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <path d="M195,475 L200,483 L205,475" stroke="currentColor"></path>
    <text x="208" y="468" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted">bindings</text>

    {/* The shared stores, bussed to both Workers down the left margin */}
    <path
      d="M6,149 L6,556 M6,149 L20,149 M6,360 L20,360 M6,556 L20,556"
      class="stroke-rule"
      stroke-dasharray="3 4"></path>
    <rect x="20" y="483" width="360" height="146" class="fill-surface" stroke="currentColor"></rect>
    <text x="32" y="509" font-size="17" class="font-mono fill-current">Shared by both Workers</text>
    <text x="32" y="535" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >D1 &#183; audit, tokens, transcripts, evals</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="554" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >KV &#183; caches and flags</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="573" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >R2 &#183; generated PDFs and documents</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="592" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >Analytics Engine &#183; request telemetry</text
    >
    <text x="32" y="611" font-size="14" class="font-mono fill-ink-muted"
      >Queue &#183; high-intent events &#8594; email</text
    >
  </svg>

  <figcaption class="mt-4 max-w-prose font-mono text-micro text-ink-muted">
    Drawn from the deployed configuration &mdash; the two <code>wrangler.jsonc</code> files and the two
    Worker entries in{' '}
    <a class="text-accent underline" href="https://github.com/ryanlindsey/ryanlindsey.me"
